HST Office: "Set As Default" in Writer's Font, Paragraph and Page Setup dialogs and in Sheets' Format Cells
and Page Setup, like the reference word processor (owner request for 1.0.2).

- SfxTabDialogController offers a "hstsetdefault" button (hidden in the .ui; a dialog shows it with
  HstShowSetDefault and answers HstDefaultQuestion/HstApplyDefault). It asks "This document only / All new
  documents" (sfx/ui/hstdefaultscopedialog.ui, all new documents preselected), then ends like OK, so the
  selection also gets the values. The values are what the dialog shows (input set plus the pages' changes),
  read without Ok(): Sheets' Ok() applies print titles.
- This document: the Default Paragraph Style (Font: font and effects; Paragraph: alignment, indents,
  spacing, line spacing, breaks without page breaks, tabs) or the Default Page Style (paper, orientation,
  margins); Sheets: the Default cell style (font, alignment; not number formats, borders, fill) or the
  Default page style (paper, margins, centering, scaling, print order). Undoable.
- All new documents: the same change is written into <profile>/user/hst/default-templates/<module>.<ext>,
  made from the module's current default template (a template the user chose stays untouched) or from a new
  empty document, saved through a temporary file and registered with SfxObjectFactory::SetStandardTemplate.
  It is outside the template folders, so new documents carry no template link and never ask to update
  styles. Templates ▸ Reset Default goes back to the built-in defaults.
- Access keys: D as in the reference (Paragraph, Page Setup); the Font tab gives D to Hidden and H to Help,
  so Font uses A; every letter of the label is taken on the Number, Alignment and Font tabs of Format Cells
  (they keep the spreadsheet's keys), so that button has none.
- New files are under MPL-2.0 like the files that use them.

License: these upstream files remain under their original license (MPL-2.0).
Test: CppunitTest_sw_uiwriter9 (testHstSetAsDefault*), CppunitTest_sc_hst_set_as_default,
tests/runtime/check-set-as-default.py.
